### 5. Information Disclosure (OWASP A01:2021 – Broken Access Control / A05:2021)

**Risk:** Medium

**Issue:** Several information leakage vectors:

```javascript
// app.js (line 6) - Detailed error/stack traces exposed
res.json({ status: 'ok', timestamp: new Date().toISOString() });

// app.js (lines 17-19) - Server version leaked in logs
console.log('Server running on port 3000'); // Could leak more info
```

**Recommendation:** Implement centralized error handling:

```javascript
// SECURE: Global error handler
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  // Log full error server-side only
  console.error('Error:', {
    message: err.message,
    stack: err.stack,
    path: req.path,
    method: req.method,
    ip: req.ip,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
  });

  // Send generic message to client
  const isDev = process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development';
  res.status(err.status || 500).json({
    error: isDev ? err.message : 'Internal server error',
    ...(isDev && { stack: err.stack }) // Only in dev
  });
});

// Remove version from headers
app.disable('x-powered-by');
```

